{"title":"Career roadmap — Cartographer","role":"Cartographer","summary":"A Cartographer creates, analyses and maintains maps and geospatial visualisations using geographic data, satellite imagery, GIS, remote sensing and spatial analysis. Modern cartography goes far beyond drawing maps—it combines geography + GIS + data + design + technology.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Geography"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Cartographers can work in government mapping, urban planning, surveying, environmental management, defence, disaster management, infrastructure, logistics, location intelligence and geospatial technology companies."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build geography, GIS, cartographic design, spatial data and remote-sensing foundations"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in GIS, remote sensing, urban mapping, environmental mapping, infrastructure or location intelligence"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress to GIS Specialist, Senior Cartographer, Geospatial Analyst or Geospatial Project Lead"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead geospatial programmes, mapping platforms, spatial-data teams or geospatial technology projects"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Geography & mapping foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical geography"},{"text":"Human geography"},{"text":"Economic geography"},{"text":"Regional geography"},{"text":"Map reading"},{"text":"Coordinate systems"},{"text":"Latitude and longitude"},{"text":"Scale and projections"},{"text":"Topographic maps"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Geographic data concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Spatial reasoning"},{"text":"Analytical thinking"},{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Technical writing"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Output","text":"Create basic thematic maps of a city, district or state."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — GIS & digital cartography"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GIS fundamentals"},{"text":"Spatial databases"},{"text":"Vector and raster data"},{"text":"Georeferencing"},{"text":"Digitisation"},{"text":"Coordinate Reference Systems"},{"text":"Map projections"},{"text":"Spatial queries"},{"text":"Geospatial data formats"},{"text":"Cartographic design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"ArcGIS Pro"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Basic SQL"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Choropleth maps"},{"text":"Point maps"},{"text":"Heat maps"},{"text":"Network maps"},{"text":"Land-use maps"},{"text":"Population-density maps"},{"text":"Thematic maps"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Advanced geospatial technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Build capability in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Remote sensing"},{"text":"Satellite imagery"},{"text":"Image classification"},{"text":"Spatial analysis"},{"text":"GPS/GNSS concepts"},{"text":"Web GIS"},{"text":"3D mapping"},{"text":"Drone/GIS concepts"},{"text":"Python for geospatial analysis"},{"text":"GeoPandas"},{"text":"Rasterio"},{"text":"PostGIS"},{"text":"Mapbox/Leaflet concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-year projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Strong projects could include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Urban land-use and land-cover mapping"},{"text":"Flood-risk mapping using GIS"},{"text":"Satellite-based vegetation analysis"},{"text":"Urban expansion mapping"},{"text":"Public-transport accessibility map"},{"text":"Groundwater potential mapping"},{"text":"Air-pollution spatial distribution"},{"text":"Disaster-risk mapping"},{"text":"Agricultural land-use classifi